.TH LSOF 1 "2026" "KERNEL32" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lsof \- liste les fichiers ouverts / list open files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lsof
[-p pid] [-u user] [-c cmd] [file...]
.br
.B fuser
[-vks] file...
.br
.SH DESCRIPTION
lsof prints, for every process of /proc, its working directory, executable and open descriptors with their type. fuser lists the processes using the given
files; -v is verbose, -k kills them, -s is silent. Both read /proc/PID/{status,fd,cwd,exe}.
.SH SEE ALSO
ps(1), netstat(1)
